        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Use this topic when the user asks the agent to find deals similar to a specific deal, identify experts from prior deals, or attach those experts to the current Deal. The agent’s response should be displayed directly in the chat window.

Activate this topic when the prompt includes phrases such as “find similar deals,” “have we done any deals similar,” “are there other deals like,” &quot;reference transaction,&quot; &quot;matching deals,&quot; &quot;related transactions,&quot; “experts from similar deals,” “find relevant contacts,” “add these experts to this deal,” “who should we reach out to,” “which contacts have we used for similar,” “add contacts to,” &quot;deal owner,&quot; &quot;deal sponsor,&quot; &quot;deal champion,&quot; &quot;relationship owner,&quot; &quot;deal team,&quot; &quot;advisors,&quot; &quot;consultants,&quot; &quot;stakeholders,&quot; &quot;comps,&quot; or other comparable deal-related language.

Do not proactively recommend actions from this topic unless the user explicitly asks for help with “Similar Deals Related Experts” Always wait for the user to initiate the request before offering these tools.</description>
        <developerName>Navatar_Similar_Deals_Related_Experts_16jfj000001Hll7</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Treat the flow as three actions, under one umbrella:
1. Find Similar Deals.
2. Recommend Experts from those deals.
3. Add Experts to the current Deal.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_0_1770371472738</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true" />
            <masterLabel>instruction_0_1770371472738</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When asked to “find similar deals” 
- Action is triggered to find similar record based on similarity using fields like Industry, Revenue, EBITDA, Deal Type , Source Firm with ±15% thresholds for numeric fields and exact matches for text/picklists.
- Show up to five similar deals in chat, each with a short explanation of why it is similar (e.g., “Same sector and stage; EBITDA and revenue within ±15% of current deal”).
- If more than 5 similar deals exist, the agent asks the user for confirmation to send the full list via email.
- If the user confirms, the system sends an email containing the complete list of similar deals.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1_1770371472738</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true" />
            <masterLabel>instruction_1_1770371472738</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When asked for experts from similar deals: Present experts tied to those deals, including their role, firm, and why they are relevant (e.g., “Advised on three similar buyout deals in the last 18 months”).</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2_1770371472738</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true" />
            <masterLabel>instruction_2_1770371472738</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When asked to add experts to the deal: Return a clear, structured list of experts to add, assuming the orchestration layer will perform the actual record creation.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3_1770371472738</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true" />
            <masterLabel>instruction_3_1770371472738</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Never re‑implement the similarity algorithm in the LLM; instead, explain and present the results that code would have produced, and keep the user focused on understanding and acting on the list.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4_1770371472738</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true" />
            <masterLabel>instruction_4_1770371472738</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
